e unless direct prebiotic closure to the aldehyde is shown.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P6\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.92,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.87\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.9,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.92,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.79,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.96,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.87,\n      \"feedback\": \"This is the most chemically secure subroute in the network. From imidazole-4-acetaldehyde onward, the Strecker and aminonitrile hydrolysis logic is standard and well aligned with the Shen closure step, though this pathway does not address how the imidazole aldehyde is supplied.\",\n      \"approved\": true,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Mark P6 clearly as a late-stage subroute rather than a complete synthesis from simple feedstocks.\",\n        \"Add explicit hydrolysis stoichiometry and conditions for rxn_008.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P7\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.5,\n        \"rxn_009\": 0.57\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.6,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.69,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.56,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.84,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.62,\n      \"feedback\": \"The one-pot histidine observation is literature-backed, but the compressed net representation is too loose. rxn_009 omits NH3 even though the Shen 1990 closure uses ammonia in the Strecker stage, so the edge should be treated as an empirical aggregate rather than a faithful mechanistic net reaction.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_001\",\n        \"rxn_009\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Rewrite rxn_009 to include NH3 or explicitly label it as an empirical aggregate of the Shen 1990 mixture.\",\n        \"Avoid presenting the compressed net edge as mechanistically equival