y aligned with the Ni-catalyzed CO/H2/NH3 experiments, including the fact that histidine itself was reported. But rxn_009 is an unresolved high-temperature surface-catalytic source term, not an elementary step to histidine, and the network omits the important temperature and catalyst metadata. Keep it as a literature-backed aggregate route only.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_009\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Annotate rxn_009 as unresolved multistep Fischer-Tropsch-type chemistry.\",\n        \"Add Ni catalyst and temperature metadata, roughly 200-700 C in the cited work.\",\n        \"Do not imply identified histidine-specific intermediates unless supporting data are added.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P8\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_010\": 0.59\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.60,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.53,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.61,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.65,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.60,\n      \"feedback\": \"Same overall assessment as P7, but for alumina catalysis. Endpoint support exists in the older Fischer-Tropsch-type literature, yet no histidine-specific intermediate sequence is known and the environmental conditions are under-specified. This branch works as a coarse source term, not as a resolved mechanism.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_010\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Annotate rxn_010 as unresolved multistep Fischer-Tropsch-type chemistry.\",\n        \"Add alumina catalyst and temperature metadata.\",\n        \"Keep this branch clearly separated from the mechanistically resolved Shen route.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P9\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_011\": 0.58\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.59,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.52,\n      \"environmental_progressi